<?xml version="1.0"?>
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <section id="commercekings_notification">
            <group id="slack" translate="label comment" sortOrder="60" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0">
                <label>Slack</label>
                <fieldset_css>commercekings-config-section</fieldset_css>
                <comment>Messages to your team's Slack channels through your own Slack app: create it from the manifest in the module's README (scopes chat:write and chat:write.public), install it to your workspace and paste its Bot User OAuth Token here.</comment>
                <field id="bot_token" translate="label comment" type="obscure" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Bot token</label>
                    <backend_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Backend\Encrypted</backend_model>
                    <comment>Starts with xoxb-. Stored encrypted.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="test_channel_id" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Test channel ID</label>
                    <comment>Where "Send test message" posts, e.g. C0123ABCD: in Slack, open the channel's details; the ID is at the bottom. Features that post to Slack have their own channel settings.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="test_message" translate="label comment" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Test</label>
                    <frontend_model>CommerceKings\NotificationSlack\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\TestButton</frontend_model>
                    <comment>Save first: the test uses the saved token and channel of this scope.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
